  "id": "lateral-thalamic-nucleus",
  "term": "lateral thalamic nucleus",
  "definition": "The lateral thalamic nucleus is a thalamic brain region discussed here as part of speech-motor control circuitry. In this study, the left ventral lateral thalamic nucleus was part of a feedforward control network, and weaker connectivity between it and the right anterior cerebellum was linked with speech blocks in adults who stutter.",
